{"author":"did:key:z6Mkmz8SWiUshwDMszSqwzMngt7ScNmsEj7vZoFRLjpcZTm9","evaluation":{"digest":{"sha256":"ec2a9d63d5cf029246c48002b739b35caa63380574c4ee9bdf19bc4e8bf5f179"}},"instructions":"Return exactly ACCEPT or REJECT.","network.jinn.binary-judgment.item-sha256":"sha256:fa1023d397cc0a064d87f5431ed24c0920b693b22afc2fe2aee1504b88fecf77","outputs":[{"mediaType":"text/plain; charset=utf-8","name":"judge-response","required":true},{"mediaType":"application/vnd.jinn.binary-judgment.observation.v1+json","name":"judge-observation","required":true},{"mediaType":"application/vnd.inspect-ai.eval-log+json","name":"inspect-log","required":false}],"payload":{"candidateAnswer":"Mexico, Iceland","evidence":"[D16:9 | 5:13 pm on 9 July, 2022] James: I also love to read, especially while snuggled under the covers on a cold winter day. But now it’s summer and I want something more exciting! By the way, I bought air tickets to Toronto, and I’m leaving the day after tomorrow evening.\n[D17:22 | 9:49 am on 22 July, 2022] James: Everything went great! In addition, I even managed to get out to another country. The city of Nuuk, if you know. I stayed there quite a bit, but at least I had one more country to add to my bucket list!","itemId":"urn:uuid:20789e01-0866-5b06-9ede-7fdd9047c039","provenance":{"sourceCommitment":"sha256:d17316a7cb0f28d660f8427b36761e534412386c39834c6b2d35a76d0f2bdfb1","timestamp":"2026-04-02T14:22:55Z"},"question":"Which countries did James visit in July 2022?","referenceAnswer":"Canada, Greenland","sources":[{"digest":{"sha256":"d17316a7cb0f28d660f8427b36761e534412386c39834c6b2d35a76d0f2bdfb1"}}]},"profile":{"digest":{"sha256":"ebb34d8362e2cc3135847a5ad6f3ee3d9c2d9922a2b827aa9dfcbaf440b22557"},"uri":"https://spec.jinn.network/task-profiles/binary-judgment/2.0"},"protocol":"https://spec.jinn.network/profiles/task-execution/v1"}